 "content_notes": "Tone: remarkable and ironic. Andrew C. Thornton II (deceased 1985) appears only as a faceless silhouette tagged NOT A LIKENESS; his fall and his body are never shown (the resident's reaction is shown, not what he sees). The bear is shown alive (frames 1 and last) and is never shown dead, hurt or suffering; its death is stated in words only. No loose drugs (plain wrapped packets), no weapon, no violence. Investigators, the resident, the deputy, the partner and the hiker are generic figures, never named; no badge, crest or insignia of any real force or agency, no aircraft registration. 'Gucci' and the 2023 film 'Cocaine Bear' appear only as plain typed words: no logo, poster or artwork. The stuffed bear's authenticity is disputed, so the narration says 'said to be'. The statistic and lesson cards name their sources. Every card is our own typed graphic. No dialogue is invented. Status verified 2026-10-16.",
